WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.430
You guys weren't able to reverse the scores but did enough.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.820
You all pass the tryout.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.240
We did it!

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.490
We really did it!

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.490
Yeah.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.570
Oh, however,

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.410
there's an exception for one of you.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.250
Goro Shigeno.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.760
You'll be joining the Majors group on the main field next door.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.780
WHAT!?

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.030
This is the locker room.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.560
So this is a Major League locker room!

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.700
Your locker is...

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.600
that one over on the left at the end.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.980
Cool!

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.850
You've already written my name!

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.500
And even a uniform!

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.880
My number is 56!

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.480
This is great! Great!

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.200
Number 56 is Goro!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.430
It sort of looks like my name!

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.140
You've arranged a good number for me.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.490
Very thank you!

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.350
Old man!

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:52.360
We also got a glove and cleats for you, since you lost your own through theft.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.720
Please use these.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:54.890
Glove?

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:55.940
Cleats?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.030
I can have these too?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:04.420
Just what you'd expect from the Majors; you're really generous!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.500
Anyway,

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.820
when you've changed, go to the main field.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.710
I should go to the main field?

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.780
Okay, okay!

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.170
<i>However...</i>

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:20.300
<i>To put such a rookie in the Major League camp right off the bat...</i>

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:24.900
<i>What was the Assistant General Manager and the scout thinking?</i>

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.650
What?

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:46.750
A Japanese pitcher who just passed the tryouts is going to join the Major League camp?

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.240
Yes, Coach.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.960
I got a call from the Assistant General Manager about it.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.180
He told me that he completely shut out the Red Rox.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.450
I see. For now, I'll leave it to you.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.580
Pursue this matter and keep me updated.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.590
I understand.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.500
<i>A Japanese pitcher?</i>

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.510
<i>Don't tell me that guy...</i>

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.870
Hey, what's the matter, Bolton?

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.800
Sorry.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.480
<i>From a testee to competing for a spot on the Major League roster right away?</i>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.530
<i>It's true that you pitch well...</i>

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:23.950
<i>But...</i>

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.240
Like usual, you send it flying far.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.960
Yo!

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.790
I've come to get my revenge without delay, Bolton-chan.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.870
<i>I thought I proved to you that it's still too early for you to come here,</i>

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.380
<i>boy.</i>

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.360
Welcome!

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.250
You are Shigeno, right?

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.030
I'm Zimmerman, the pitching coach!

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:53.420
Coach Gary has put me in charge of your training.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:55.020
Are you okay?

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:00.890
Hey, Fox!

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:03.810
Come over here for a second!

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.280
You wanted something?

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.570
If I remember correctly, you know some Japanese, right?

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.290
Can you translate for me?

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.830
Yeah, no problem.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.610
Who is that Asian?

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:18.540
Dunno.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.720
This is the pitching coach, Zimmerman.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:26.130
He says that he has heard that you're a rookie who just passed the tryout yesterday.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.060
You can speak Japanese?

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:29.800
Yeah.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:34.010
Because of my father's work, I spent five years in Japan when I was a kid.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.310
Whenever you don't understand something or want advice,

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.660
you can ask him, through me, he says.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.990
Okay, I'll leave you to it.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:44.900
Okay.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.640
He'll notify you about who's taking the mound for a game up until the day before the game.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.500
And also,

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.120
unlike in Japan, we don't have a regimen of obligatory activities here.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.070
The people who come here know how to regulate their training themselves.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.210
Do as you wish, rookie.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.630
Well, that's how it is.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.730
H-Hey! Wait a minute!

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:11.030
Is that all!?

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.680
You're abandoning the newcomer?

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.100
Just kidding.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.970
I see.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.520
Just what you'd expect from the land of the free, America.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.920
Well,

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.940
it's just what I had hoped for.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:29.610
I didn't come this far...

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.410
thinking I would try to get advice from others.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.340
They're at it! They're at it!

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.610
Just what you'd expect from the Majors, right?

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.380
They're throwing well.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.340
Oh? Wow!

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.900
You're a catcher?

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:56.870
Yeah.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:00.350
A bullpen catcher who jumps between the Majors and Minors though.

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.840
Have you warmed up?

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.070
Y-Yeah.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.480
In that case, I'll catch for you.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.510
Thank you!

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:11.630
Your face looks like Frankenstein's, but...

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.200
you're a good person.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.380
Let's get along!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.100
Uh...

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.360
Fox.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:18.450
Okay!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.370
Okay!

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:28.670
It's okay.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.340
I pitched quite a lot yesterday.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.570
Also, today is my first day too.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.600
I'll just cruise around...

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.400
carefully!

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:47.690
<i>I see.</i>

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.510
<i>He's got speed.</i>

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:49.510
Dang.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:50.820
It's not flying fast.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.200
I guess my shoulder really is heavy today.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:57.990
Hey, Norton.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.050
Catch for me.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:07:59.910
Okay.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.120
Sanchez.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.840
Move.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.500
Huh?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.720
This is my reserved spot.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.130
Huh?

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.650
What?

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.780
You don't understand English?

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:17.740
Look,

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.560
I'm telling you to hurry up and move, boy.

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:24.130
I don't know what you're saying, but...

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.260
I was throwing here first.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.770
You, wait, understand?

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.400
That idiot!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.430
You!

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:40.110
Don't take me lightly, damn fish!

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:44.120
Do you lack the manners to hand over the mound to your team's ace?

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.280
Oh my, he made him angry.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.280
Hey, let's go, Norton!

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.250
Y-Yeah.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:50.800
It seems that rookie doesn't know about our untamable horse, Sanchez.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.220
As I said,

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:57.840
I-was-here-first kick!

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:01.210
A kick!?

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.020
Though he took off his cleats for the time being.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.660
Wait for your turn, mustached old man!

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:06.960
A Japanese person...

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.360
waits in line to eat his ramen!

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:12.860
Damn kid...

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.700
It's been a while since a rookie...

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.040
who's worth beating up has come here!

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:21.010
Now you've done it!

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.830
You bastard!

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.410
What are you doing!?

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:29.630
You guys! Stop them!

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.030
Enough.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:42.970
Let me go.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.160
Damn it!

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.400
It hurts!

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.830
You were the one who attacked first!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.980
Stop this foolishness, Shigeno!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:54.330
The situation is that you're allowed to be at this camp because of your Minor League contract.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.600
Try to restrain yourself a little!

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.380
You're taking on our ace, Sanchez!

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.400
But...!

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:00.760
Let him go.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:08.000
I like you.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.080
What?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:16.010
If a rookie wants to survive here, he must have some pride and not just give up the mound to a stranger.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:21.220
Well, the number of prideful rookies has increased a lot recently.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.900
S-Sanchez...

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:28.150
I'm done already, so you can pitch here.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:28.800
No.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:31.160
I don't feel like pitching here anymore.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.000
Norton!

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.740
Let's go to the indoor bullpen.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:35.400
Wait.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:38.900
Don't run away, old man.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:47.370
Are you so afraid that if we pitch next to one another,
your dull old-fashioned pitch will hit the mitt later than a rookie's?

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.500
Well!?

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.130
Hey, Fox.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.870
Translate what I just said.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:55.350
Don't joke around! I won't translate something like that!

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:57.380
You don't have to translate it.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:02.550
I understand that he's picking a fight by the look in his eyes.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:04.280
It seems...

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:07.140
that for us to both enjoy our stay at this camp,

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:11.110
we need to make our positions clear.

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:18.060
This is a free fansub.

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:18.060
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.380
W-What's that?

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:29.450
That's a specially made iron frame that our pitchers use for practice.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:35.520
Its inside is made to be just as big as an average batter's strike zone.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:37.570
What's that?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:39.840
It's a contest of who can throw the ball through that hole?

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.790
Ridiculous! That's easy.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:46.380
He's saying that just throwing a ball through the middle of that frame is easy.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:50.180
Are you stupid? With such a simple competition,
we wouldn't know anything.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.820
We're going to hit the frame itself.

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:57.270
We're both going to throw ten pitches at that frame and see who hits it the most.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.520
Hey, Sanchez! You're being childish!

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:04.470
A veteran such as yourself shouldn't challenge a rookie like this!

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:08.160
Veteran or rookie, it doesn't matter, Mr. Zimmerman.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:12.080
If his big mouth matches the skill of the Majors,

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.250
starting tomorrow, I won't ask him to give up the mound to me.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:19.650
Okay.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:24.010
Then I'll show you my skills right away.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:34.800
H-Hey, how many times have you hit the frame?

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.630
I've only done this two or three times, but...

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.770
hitting it once every two pitches is lucky.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.190
Let's do this!

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:49.620
He hit it!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:57.330
You're gravely mistaken if you think I'm a pitcher who's got just speed and no control!

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:15.900
O-Out of ten pitches, he hit it eight times!

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:19.480
T-This guy, even with that pitching skill, he's got control too!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.690
How's that?

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.250
Come on, it's your turn next.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:26.860
Are you satisfied with that?

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.330
You learn where your limits are, Minor Leaguer!?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.250
W-What's that!?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.730
W-What's that!?

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:33.800
Move.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:38.630
Let's see...

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:43.050
In that case, I'll show you how it's done in the Majors.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:01.860
You're showing off and then you miss right away!

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.300
This is too good!

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.320
Hey, Norton!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.580
That iron frame is two centimeters too far to the left!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:14.310
Which one of us is making poor excuses and is full of pride?

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:16.080
S-Sorry!

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.000
It really is off its position by one or two centimeters!

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:22.540
It seems like the iron frame really was off its position a bit.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.540
I'll start with informing you:

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:29.160
by no means do I aim for that frame when I throw.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.050
The place where my foot steps on the rubber...

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.430
The location and angle of my foot when I take a step forward,

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.680
and the 60 feet and 6 inches to the 17-inch wide white home plate.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:44.020
My body knows them down to the inch.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:49.610
It's so I can control whether my pitch hits the strike zone half a ball too far out or not at will. {AKA, he can change exactly if the pitch becomes a Ball or is within the strike zone}

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:56.200
In other words, as long as that frame has been set up in the same way as the strike zone...

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:00.750
it doesn't matter if it's a breaking ball...

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.170
or any kind of pitch;

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:06.170
they all inevitably hit.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.310
And this is why...

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:13.890
my body remembers the feeling of steering the ball precisely into the corner.

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:21.810
However, it's not something even a Minor Leaguer of your level can do by vaguely hitting.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.020
Do you understand...

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.030
what the real thing is?

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.700
<i>He...</i>

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:40.120
<i>He's steering them all to the outside of the frame!</i>

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.090
Nine out of ten pitches...

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.060
Even if it's just a small one point difference, you lose, Señor.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:01.480
Now that you know your place, you'll act accordingly, right?

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:08.110
<i>It's a complete defeat.</i>

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.050
<i>It's not just a one point difference.</i>

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:12.350
<i>That old man...</i>

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:16.540
<i>Both his technique and accuracy are miles better than someone like me.</i>

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:22.040
<i>And unlike my pitches, which I desperately tried to locate to the place I wanted,</i>

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:29.950
<i>Sanchez exhibited perfect control in his pitching.</i>

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:33.010
<i>This is...</i>

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.270
<i>the Majors.</i>

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:47.500
Shigeno, are you still here?

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.120
Y-Yeah.

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:48.980
Y-Yeah.

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:54.360
I bring word from the Coach.

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:58.280
In the exhibition game the day after tomorrow, it seems you'll be the starting pitcher.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:01.520
"Get ready," he said.

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.610
Okay! One more!

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:07.900
Six, four, three!

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:08.190
Six, four, three!

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:08.920
Six, four, three!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.930
Okay, that's good! Continue like that!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:16.830
Next:

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:17.120
Five, four, three!

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:17.300
Five, four, three!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.080
Five, four, three!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.330
Big sister!

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.910
Oh, Taiga?

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:23.640
You're still loafing around here?

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:27.830
I've been accepted to my university already,
and I've been buried in exams so I wanted some exercise.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:28.810
You got a problem with that?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.980
It's not a problem or anything, but...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:35.290
I feel pity for my big sister, who doesn't even have a single plan for a date on her day off.

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:35.780
W-What's that!?

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.830
W-What's that!?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:43.180
It seems like Shigeno-senpai passed the test for some baseball team in America.

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:43.750
Huh?

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:47.670
Even though it's only been three days since he went to America.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.880
That old man sure is great.

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:56.970
<i>Honda.</i>

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.010
<i>It won't work like that.</i>

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:16.070
I'm telling you your variety of pitches and control are absolutely not Major League level.

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.120
It was a dream.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:42.760
Can I sit here?

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:44.850
Fox.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.910
What's the matter?

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.810
You seem awfully gloomy.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:50.230
Are you nervous about being the starting pitcher tomorrow?

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.480
Well, I don't know about that.

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.280
Our opponent tomorrow is the Dallas Elephants.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.260
It's a team that hits well, but...

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:03.410
at this time, they'll most likely not play their best players.

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:08.450
I've been told that I'll be one of the starting players tomorrow too.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:12.630
If it's possible, I'd like to get through the game without the opponent scoring any earned runs off the pitcher.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:15.670
That's impossible.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:17.840
You think so too, right?

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:22.570
No matter how much of a lead I get, someone at my level isn't suited for being in the Majors.

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:26.390
Is that why you're gloomy? You're still thinking about your loss to Sanchez?

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.470
Don't worry about that.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:32.730
Your opponent was one of the best in the Majors-

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.730
Please stop trying to comfort me.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:36.650
Everyone watching noticed the evident difference in skill between me and Sanchez.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:41.610
Then why am I participating in this fight for a roster spot?

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:46.280
Why did the guys at the top make me join the Majors camp?

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.450
I'm unsightly!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.700
Bolton hitting my pitch was not a fluke!

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:58.270
If this is how it is, I can see with my own eyes that they'll hit my pitches when I stand on the mound tomorrow.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:03.160
If I know they'll hit my pitches, I can't start.

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:04.330
I'll think of a strategy to compensate for this,

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:09.000
so please translate to the coach to change the date when I take the mound to a free game in the second half!

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.460
Please, Fox!

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:11.610
That's absurd.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:14.580
Tell him through gestures yourself.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.920
H-Hey, Fox!

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:17.730
Wait a minute!

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.610
Come on, it shouldn't be too much trouble to just translate for me!

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.070
Stop joking around!

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:24.910
What do you mean by "change the date when you'll take the mound"?

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.410
If you're so scared of having your pitches hit,

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.800
volunteer to drop down to the Minors yourself!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.030
Listen!

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:36.680
Everyone here is fighting desperately to get a spot on the 25 man roster!

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:42.300
Also, the Minors is crawling with guys who haven't gotten an opportunity as good as you, but they're still doing their best!

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.130
I'm like that too!

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:49.510
Without being patted on the shoulder, all we think about is taking the chance we've been offered and producing results!

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:54.140
Most of the time during the season is taken up by games and riding buses long distances. 

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:57.220
Having a low salary and not being able to choose where to live. 

00:20:57.220 --> 00:21:00.480
Just eating hamburgers and hot dogs every day.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:06.530
Everyone's experienced that Minor League lifestyle and finally made it here!

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:09.910
You're too naive!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.240
Why is someone like you here?

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.940
That's what I want to know!

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:55.900
I-It's useless.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:56.910
I-It's useless.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:00.720
After all, with just one day of trying to throw at that spot...

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:05.340
I won't be able to match up to Sanchez's powerful control at all!

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:10.330
<i>If you're so scared of having your pitches hit,</i>

00:22:10.330 --> 00:22:12.390
<i>volunteer to drop down to the Minors yourself!</i>

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:17.760
<i>You're too naive!</i>

00:22:23.390 --> 00:22:25.870
Get hit and go to the Minors, huh?

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:29.620
If I don't have enough power, then it can't be helped, I guess.

00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:12.460
A big stadium...

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:13.900
And this huge audience!

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:14.890
Too cool!

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:17.220
The Majors' mound is too cool!

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:20.770
I don't know how far my strength will carry me, but...

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:22.180
I'll go as far as I can!

00:24:22.180 --> 00:24:23.270
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:25.150
The Guidepost Towards the World!

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:27.780
Run to the stage of your dreams!
